AB  - Northrop Grumman is developing a new technology network that may soon allow US soldiers engaged in urban warfare access to real-time surveillance. The technology known as HURT was recently tested in a training exercise that took place in a simulated urban combat zone at the Marine Corps Air Ground Combat Center, California. HURT which stands for Heterogehous urban RSTA team is a system that can prioritize and respond to requests for information on enemy positions and can also autonomously direct unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV). Northrop Grumman's initial contract awarded in January 2005 and worth USD11.6 million is coming to an end and is considering an additional contract. According to sources HURT can be deployed in combat by 2008.
