AB  - The UK's Special Air Service (SAS) Regiment has carried out trials of the Mission Technologies backpack unmanned surveillance targeting and enhanced reconnaissance (BUSTER) small unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) ahead of an enhanced deployment of UK special forces personnel to Afghanistan in year 2006. The BUSTER is launched by a small catapult and recovered by parachute. It has a payload capacity of 1.4 kg for electro-optical/infra-red surveillance equipment. The Joint UAV Experimentation Programme (JUEP) team used the BUSTER during urban warfare trials in year 2004 and it has also been trialled by the US Army.
