AB  - Rafael Armament Development Authority has unveiled a portable, lighter weight versions of its Spotlite electro-optic small-arms detection system. The Spotlite Mk-2, is designed for use by dismounted infantry and special forces at platoon, company, and battalion level in reconnaissance and urban warfare missions. The original system comprises a forward-looking infrared camera, a continuous zoom charge-coupled device (CCD), a laser range-finder, a commander and multiple networked friendly sniper end stations. This system, which uses a generator as its main power source was considered very heavy and complex for certain IDF requirements. The spotlite Mk-2 translates data into co-ordinates for counter users and counter-capability platforms, including helicopters and main battle tanks. The system also includes a stop and stare facility, where real-time information is co-displayed alongside memory to provide an intelligence gathering or dissemination capability for a particular scenario.
