AB  - It has been claimed that wargames save lives. This chapter examines the extent to which wargaming can be used to support the planning and analysis through the three just war considerations of jus ad bellum, jus in bello and jus post bellum. The chapter argues that wargaming can make a significant contribution to the examination of just war considerations, both within the professional military community and beyond. The chapter begins by describing what constitutes wargaming and how it is used by the military and others. The chapter then explores how AI could be used in wargaming, and how urban warfare, and by extension urban wargaming, provide the in extremis case for studying just war and wargaming. The main body of the chapter then examines the role of wargaming, and AI in support of war and wargaming, in each of three elements of a just war analysis. The chapter concludes by arguing the case for a broader use both of wargaming in considering just war issues, and in including just war issues within wargames, and by highlighting the need for just wargames to support just wars. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Maria Power and Maggi Savin-Baden; individual chapters, the contributors.
